```spl
`SOC Lab Detection Rule`
`Rule Name: Linux SSH Authentication Brute-Force Detection`
`Data Source: linux_auth | index=blue`
`MITRE ATT&CK: T1110.001 (Password Guessing)`
`Severity: High (>= 100 attempts) / Medium (>= 20 attempts) / Low (>= 5 attempts)`
`Description: Parses SSH failure lines from auth.log via regex, aggregates failures by host and source IP, and triggers when failures >= 5.`
```

index=blue sourcetype=linux_auth "Failed password"
| rex "Failed password for (?:(?:invalid user )?)(?<user>\S+) from (?<src_ip>\S+)"
| stats count AS failed_attempts values(user) AS targeted_users earliest(_time) AS first_seen latest(_time) AS last_seen by host src_ip
| where failed_attempts >= 5
| eval severity=case(failed_attempts>=100,"HIGH",failed_attempts>=20,"MEDIUM",true(),"LOW")
| convert ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)
| sort 0 - failed_attempts
